WEBVTT

01:32.518 --> 01:35.220
I want women, but there's
nothing but cows here!

01:35.220 --> 01:38.490
We're about to arrive
in a charming place

01:38.490 --> 01:40.292
where things won't seem
so black and white.

01:40.292 --> 01:41.759
What do you mean by that?

01:43.595 --> 01:45.563
What?! What is that place?

01:46.498 --> 01:50.434
Isn't it amazing? It's Technicolor
Town of Pompeii.

01:54.740 --> 01:59.370
The Little Girl From the Technicolor Town

02:08.287 --> 02:09.988
And Mr. Drambuie makes another
killing on the auction block

02:09.988 --> 02:11.353
as he takes this new item home!

02:18.030 --> 02:19.497
Another killing?!

02:23.702 --> 02:27.798
Hey, how can a scruffy bird like you
command such a high amount?

02:28.407 --> 02:30.568
I'm much more handsome than you.

02:31.009 --> 02:32.442
How rude!

02:32.911 --> 02:33.679
A girl?!

02:33.679 --> 02:37.240
Hey, if you're here to steal something,
can you steal this girl next, please?

02:37.616 --> 02:39.083
Which girl?

02:47.793 --> 02:49.895
Why don't we start the auction
at ten thousand gold coins?

02:49.895 --> 02:50.829
13,000!

02:50.829 --> 02:51.496
15,000!
13,000!

02:51.496 --> 02:52.331
15,000!
17,000!

02:52.331 --> 02:53.131
17,000!

02:53.131 --> 02:54.633
19,000!

02:54.633 --> 02:55.801
21,000!

02:55.801 --> 02:57.894
25,000! No, 28,000!

03:00.973 --> 03:02.440
40,000...

03:15.254 --> 03:16.721
What the?!

03:25.664 --> 03:27.131
Hey what do you guys
think you're doing?!

03:27.466 --> 03:28.933
Run!

03:32.404 --> 03:33.871
Oh, no!

03:38.010 --> 03:41.070
Hey cutie pie, hold on to my hand!

03:49.054 --> 03:50.521
I can't...

04:16.715 --> 04:20.845
Kir! Hold them back for me.
This is only a painter's truck.

04:31.897 --> 04:35.230
Another day and my hands are again
stained with the color of blood.

04:51.850 --> 04:53.317
What would you have me do, Sir?

04:53.719 --> 04:57.655
She belongs to me. Find them quickly!

05:07.632 --> 05:09.099
We'll be safe here.

05:09.534 --> 05:14.665
Drambuie will never think to look
for us in his own basement.

05:15.307 --> 05:18.470
Is Drambuie the jerk that won
that last auction?

05:18.877 --> 05:22.904
Yes, he is in charge of Pompeii,
this modern art town.

05:23.482 --> 05:25.250
His real job is a paint manufacturer,

05:25.250 --> 05:27.013
but he's also a famous art collector.

05:27.519 --> 05:30.113
So why in the world was this girl
being auctioned off?

05:30.389 --> 05:33.324
I mean, I realize her beauty surpasses
any painting, but...

05:33.692 --> 05:36.217
It is my father's fault.

05:39.765 --> 05:44.065
Hey cutie pie, if it wasn't for me,
you would have been done for!

05:44.669 --> 05:47.372
Oh, Fino, I'm glad you're okay.

05:47.372 --> 05:48.839
What do you mean, your father's fault?

05:55.680 --> 05:58.240
Cutie pie, hurry up and
show me some love!

06:05.590 --> 06:11.085
I was made to be both human
and a work of art.

06:21.373 --> 06:23.275
You haven't found them yet?

06:23.275 --> 06:23.942
No, Sir.

06:23.942 --> 06:24.776
No, Sir.
I want to be sure and have her
in my collection.

06:24.776 --> 06:27.074
I want to be sure and have her
in my collection.

06:27.579 --> 06:31.242
She is the final masterpiece of
Van Kuot, the heretic painter.

06:32.317 --> 06:36.054
My father, Van Kuot, was
a legendary painter,

06:36.054 --> 06:38.989
famous for turning anything and
everything into his canvas.

06:39.691 --> 06:45.357
He painted on everything, paper,
cloth, stones and even animals.

06:45.764 --> 06:48.392
Soon, the whole world began
to take interest in his work.

06:50.001 --> 06:53.232
I, too, am one of my father's
greatest pieces.

06:55.841 --> 06:59.511
Your father turned you into an even
more beautiful work of art!

06:59.511 --> 07:00.645
I love it!

07:00.645 --> 07:03.580
I am also one of Van Kuot's
works of art.

07:04.683 --> 07:06.150
Oh, really?

07:06.785 --> 07:08.616
So you are Van Kuot's daughter?

07:09.221 --> 07:10.922
You knew about her?

07:10.922 --> 07:13.117
Those amazing colors are so beautiful.

07:13.792 --> 07:17.319
He used every color of the rainbow,
like on a tropical bird.

07:17.729 --> 07:19.526
Its beauty is unsurpassed.

07:20.866 --> 07:24.768
There is one piece that they say
is his greatest work ever.

07:25.170 --> 07:29.038
It is a vision that no one
has ever seen.

07:29.941 --> 07:31.877
That piece is supposedly unfinished

07:31.877 --> 07:34.072
and still stashed away in his studio.

07:34.779 --> 07:36.644
This says that it is called
The Painter's Self.

07:37.415 --> 07:40.782
The painting that utilizes every
last color known to the world.

07:41.486 --> 07:44.080
That's amazing. What a treasure!

07:44.489 --> 07:45.390
I'm sure it is.

07:45.390 --> 07:47.025
Hey, you work on stealing that

07:47.025 --> 07:48.788
while I work on stealing Fino's heart.

07:50.795 --> 07:52.422
My father abandoned me!

07:54.799 --> 07:58.003
He abandoned me and my mother
to further his art.

07:58.003 --> 07:59.937
He abandoned us.

08:03.375 --> 08:05.070
In preparation for making history's
greatest painting,

08:05.777 --> 08:07.301
he left us all alone.

08:08.213 --> 08:10.282
He knew where to find all
the colors of the world.

08:10.282 --> 08:12.113
Colors that, before then, had
never been made into paint.

08:13.018 --> 08:16.419
He left on a journey in search of
ideal colors to be used for paint.

08:18.924 --> 08:21.415
We waited, but he never returned.

08:22.427 --> 08:24.691
We helplessly went on a journey
of our own looking for him.

08:33.438 --> 08:35.906
But during the trip...

08:39.744 --> 08:43.407
Mommy, mommy! Mommy!

08:55.160 --> 08:58.288
Why haven't you tried to
destroy that painting?

09:04.869 --> 09:06.336
Is someone back there?!

09:07.005 --> 09:09.997
It's you! Hey, they're over here!
It's Kuot's daughter!

09:16.815 --> 09:18.305
Kir Royale!

09:36.001 --> 09:37.802
You guys playing tag?

09:37.802 --> 09:39.463
Games are good every once
in a while, you know?

09:39.938 --> 09:43.669
The key to his last masterpiece
lives inside her memory.

09:53.084 --> 09:54.551
They're over here!

10:09.834 --> 10:11.358
Damn! Where could they have gone?!

10:17.442 --> 10:18.643
Sorry about that.

10:18.643 --> 10:21.635
That jerk Drambuie always
has to be so harsh.

10:22.247 --> 10:24.582
Ever since he took over Pompeii,

10:24.582 --> 10:27.278
the black market has continued
to grow and grow.

10:27.986 --> 10:29.921
It's all just so he can buy more art.

10:29.921 --> 10:31.616
It's all a waste if you ask me.

10:32.457 --> 10:34.584
Oh yeah, that hits the spot!

10:34.993 --> 10:36.928
Stay away from that fire, unless
you want to be yakitori.

10:36.928 --> 10:39.197
I don't think I could eat Kir even
if he was double deep fried.

10:39.197 --> 10:40.664
Shut up!

10:54.079 --> 10:55.680
We used to laugh

10:55.680 --> 10:58.706
sitting in front of the fire,
mother and father too.

11:02.287 --> 11:04.346
It was snowing everywhere.

11:09.060 --> 11:11.255
Mommy, mommy...

11:11.763 --> 11:13.230
What is it, Fino?

11:23.942 --> 11:27.207
Mommy, mommy!

11:29.147 --> 11:31.172
It'll be all right.

11:32.016 --> 11:33.483
Please don't cry, Fino.

11:35.687 --> 11:37.154
Fino...

11:47.098 --> 11:48.833
Fino, aren't you cold?

11:48.833 --> 11:51.569
Shall I warm you up a bit?

11:51.569 --> 11:52.871
So cold!

11:52.871 --> 11:56.307
So Kuot's studio was a little
north of Pompeii?

11:56.775 --> 11:59.938
I don't remember much more
than walking far to the south.

12:00.411 --> 12:02.208
I think I can find it then.

12:18.329 --> 12:19.430
Do not allow them to escape.

12:19.430 --> 12:22.228
I cannot allow any of Kuot's work
to fall into anyone else's hands.

12:36.881 --> 12:39.417
This house has ice all
over it, doesn't it?

12:39.417 --> 12:41.152
Oh, it's so cold!

12:41.152 --> 12:43.848
It seems like this is the coldest
place in the world.

12:45.256 --> 12:47.559
It's too bad I don't see a chimney.

12:47.559 --> 12:49.026
Let's hurry up and get inside.

12:51.863 --> 12:53.330
Welcome home.

12:53.965 --> 12:57.401
I feel like I'm walking into this house
for the first time.

13:06.711 --> 13:09.202
My mom used to like to raise birds.

13:09.981 --> 13:12.074
She used to keep them
all in this room.

13:13.251 --> 13:17.654
But after my father went away
she set them all free.

13:20.291 --> 13:22.156
Were you the only one that stayed?

13:22.827 --> 13:26.729
Not too much longer
after that, we left too.

13:30.969 --> 13:32.804
So this is where the masterpiece
is supposed to be?

13:32.804 --> 13:34.431
I don't even see one painting!

13:35.807 --> 13:40.403
It's just dark and cold in here.
If I remember correctly, then...

13:46.985 --> 13:50.477
Trompe-I'oeil... I think we've
found our painting.

13:50.955 --> 13:53.685
Painting? That looks like
a sculpture to me.

13:57.161 --> 13:59.925
You'll see what I mean after I shine
some light over here.

14:00.565 --> 14:02.430
Look, the shadows aren't moving.

14:02.901 --> 14:06.037
When paint is used to
represent objects

14:06.037 --> 14:07.504
that look like they belong in real
space, it is called trompe-I'oeil.

14:08.072 --> 14:10.233
That was one of my
father's specialties.

14:19.217 --> 14:22.253
Beyond this wall, is it a heaven
full of treasures?

14:22.253 --> 14:23.845
Or simply Hell frozen over?

14:24.289 --> 14:26.052
Only the angels know for sure.

14:33.998 --> 14:35.300
Stop touching me!

14:35.300 --> 14:36.767
Who's touching you?

14:39.404 --> 14:40.871
Sorry...

14:51.649 --> 14:54.277
What was this, some kind of
Polar Bear Club contest?

14:55.219 --> 14:56.686
That's...

14:57.288 --> 14:58.755
My...

14:59.223 --> 15:00.690
My father!

15:05.063 --> 15:08.328
What's he doing here? We thought
he was on a journey.

15:08.967 --> 15:10.764
You were right, he is on a journey.

15:16.174 --> 15:18.665
This block of ice is a human
hibernation unit.

15:19.377 --> 15:20.935
It was originally made from a glacier.

15:22.213 --> 15:24.807
I'm sure Kuot must have left
on his journey.

15:25.950 --> 15:28.612
He was searching for
the color of truth.

15:29.554 --> 15:32.190
But if he found his ideal paint color,

15:32.190 --> 15:34.525
why would he come back here
and put himself to sleep?

15:34.525 --> 15:36.127
I'm freezing my beak off in here!

15:36.127 --> 15:38.152
Fino? Where's Fino?

15:39.130 --> 15:42.566
Hey you can't get lost in a maze
at this temperature! You'll die!

15:44.902 --> 15:46.369
Did we find them?

15:47.138 --> 15:48.628
Isn't that her?

15:52.276 --> 15:54.574
Is this the famous
unknown masterpiece?

15:55.913 --> 15:59.542
He turned this huge marble wall
into a painting.

16:00.084 --> 16:02.987
He used elements like
the clouds and water

16:02.987 --> 16:04.750
to make this design on the marble.
Together they unite the painting,

16:05.423 --> 16:06.724
fusing wonderful colors
from the natural world

16:06.724 --> 16:08.715
with his own unique pigments.

16:11.696 --> 16:13.498
Life and death...

16:13.498 --> 16:15.366
He tried to use all of the colors
of the world

16:15.366 --> 16:18.062
to paint all of the things
of the world.

16:20.638 --> 16:23.541
But there is no red in that painting.

16:23.541 --> 16:25.941
Hey! No one asked you, trompe-face!

16:30.148 --> 16:31.615
Kir!

16:39.791 --> 16:44.023
Wake up for me, Professor Kuot.
We need to talk

16:44.695 --> 16:47.528
about this unknown masterpiece
of yours.

16:49.233 --> 16:51.030
Unknown masterpiece?

16:52.070 --> 16:57.474
That's right. I know all about your
failed search to find the true red.

16:57.775 --> 17:01.438
That is why you went into
hibernation, isn't it?

17:02.246 --> 17:05.409
Perhaps, this is the pigment
you were looking for.

17:06.050 --> 17:09.508
This is the ultimate red paint that
I have personally refined.

17:14.125 --> 17:15.592
Kir...

17:20.865 --> 17:23.425
Now you feel like waking up,
don't you?

17:37.482 --> 17:40.246
If this is truly red, this...

17:40.718 --> 17:42.185
This kind of red is...

17:43.754 --> 17:46.814
This is the red I have been
searching for!

17:52.597 --> 17:56.134
This is the true red.
This is what red means.

17:56.134 --> 17:59.535
This room is on fire!
What are you doing?

18:36.440 --> 18:37.975
Jing...

18:37.975 --> 18:41.206
Things look bad, but my throat
has never felt better.

19:21.652 --> 19:23.119
Daddy!

19:27.625 --> 19:29.092
Daddy!

19:32.597 --> 19:34.064
Fino...

19:41.472 --> 19:42.905
Daddy!

19:46.510 --> 19:47.977
Fino...

20:10.968 --> 20:14.460
Fino, your father has left
on a new journey.

20:23.047 --> 20:26.039
You will have to wait a little while
longer before you meet again.

20:37.662 --> 20:39.152
Daddy went on a journey.

20:40.765 --> 20:42.232
That's what Jing said.

20:44.201 --> 20:46.931
Those words have run through my
head countless times since then.

20:48.072 --> 20:49.539
They will never leave me.

20:51.676 --> 20:56.306
I kept running, and I could
finally see Pompeii.

20:58.382 --> 21:02.910
Until now, I was never truly able to
see Pompeii through the snow.

21:08.759 --> 21:12.695
All around the city, they are
in mourning.

21:13.864 --> 21:17.698
The Technicolor Town has been
stripped of its color.

21:25.743 --> 21:28.974
But I will never destroy this painting.
